@@ -107,6 +107,8 @@ The writer is bounded and never makes send workers wait for stdout. Check sequen
 
 Within a native quote `raw_rpc`, `rpc_session_connect` includes DNS/TCP setup and the complete pinned MMTLS handshake through its verified NOOP reply. Their child phases are `rpc_dns_tcp_connect` and `rpc_mmtls_handshake`. Separate phases cover quote protobuf preparation, the authenticated packet, shortlink framing, HTTP-client construction, `rpc_short_http` (request construction, response status and bounded body read), MMTLS reply decoding and authenticated reply decoding/cookie installation. Within `rpc_short_http`, `rpc_short_http_headers` ends after the request returns response headers and its status is checked; `rpc_short_http_body` covers the unchanged bounded read of the complete response body. A send or status failure has no body phase. These records use the same command, intent and attempt as their parent; nested durations are not additive. Only quote sends attach this observer. Heartbeat, synchronization, login, simulator operations and other existing callers do not emit these RPC phases.
 
+An enabled native quote trace also observes the short HTTP client's actual connector as `rpc_short_http_connect`. With the current direct HTTP route, this covers its own DNS lookup and TCP connection, separately from the longlink connection. It ends before HTTP dispatch, request upload and response-header waiting finish; the remaining header interval is not a measurement of server processing alone. Each connector call has its own observation, and cancellation is incomplete rather than successful. The default path and legacy borrowed observers add no connector layer. No endpoint, address, header, body or raw-error value is recorded.
+
 `server.user.toml` follows the Linux default `~/.config/agent-wechat/server/config.toml`. `server.toml` selects the explicit container locations:
 
 | Path | Purpose |
